From: mscharged-port
Subject: Match the goalie loose-ball pickup event on LP64
Upstream-base: 9046e67aa2077a7eb4ed6e28c9df3c1d3b368f84
Classification: native compiler/ABI compatibility; same fix as GoalieSave in 0612.

LooseBallCallback finds the pickup event (0xCF84E7CD) of each goalie
loose-ball animation with (uEventID + 0x307c0000U) == 0xe7cd, which holds
only when the sum wraps at 32 bits. unsigned long is 32 bits on the Wii and
on Windows but 64 bits on Linux and macOS, where the test never matched:
every pickup, kick, trap and dive animation kept a pickup time and duration
of 0, so the goalie approached a loose ball on the ground without ever
picking it up. Natively the sum is narrowed to 32 bits, as patch 0612 does
for GoalieSave::TriggerCallback.

diff --git a/src/Game/AI/GoalieLooseBall.cpp b/src/Game/AI/GoalieLooseBall.cpp
index 1caccc8..8aa53c6 100644
--- a/src/Game/AI/GoalieLooseBall.cpp
+++ b/src/Game/AI/GoalieLooseBall.cpp
@@ -31,7 +31,11 @@ static const int gLooseBallKickAnims[3] = { 0x2, 0x3, 0x4 };
 static bool LooseBallCallback(float fTime, float fDuration,
     unsigned long uEventID, float, void* pUserData)
 {
+#if defined(MSCHARGED_NATIVE)
+    if ((u32)(uEventID + 0x307c0000U) == 0xe7cd)
+#else
     if ((uEventID + 0x307c0000U) == 0xe7cd)
+#endif
     {
         LooseBallInfo* info = (LooseBallInfo*)pUserData;
         info->mfPickupTime = fTime;
